// `#[derive(Validate)]` on a struct with no constraint would write a function that answers an
// empty list whatever it is given -- a validation that cannot fail, which is worse than no
// validation because the call site reads as though something were checked.
//
// `#[valid]` satisfies it too, since a field that cascades gives the function something to do
// without the struct carrying a rule of its own.
#[derive(Validate)]
struct E {
    name: string
}

fn main() {
    print(1)
}
